Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: gamemaster
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         adduser,
         python3 (>= 3.10),
         sudo,
         systemd
Recommends: steamcmd
Description: administration tools for game servers on Linux
 GameMaster runs game servers on Linux. A server is set up by an
 administrator with the gamemaster program, and run afterwards with one
 program per game: zomboid for Project Zomboid, valheim for Valheim.
 .
 Every server belongs to its own Linux user, which owns the installation,
 the worlds and the save games. A server runs as a systemd service of its
 own, which loads one of its worlds at a time.
 .
 A separate user may run exactly the programs of the games through sudo,
 and nothing else on the machine. That is the door an AI agent comes
 through: it can run the servers and read their logs without being able to
 touch anything around them.
 .
 SteamCMD is only needed to install a server; it comes from the non-free
 section and is therefore recommended, not required.
